+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Least Recently Used (LRU) as the cache eviction policy, with a time-to-live (TTL) of 300 seconds for cached items. Under this policy, the least recently accessed item is evicted when capacity is reached, and any item is expired after 300 seconds (5 minutes) so that stale data is purged while backend load is still reduced.
